# digits — a 8x80 sheet, ten 8x8 cells stacked vertically.
#
# Vertical rather than the more usual horizontal strip, for one reason: a horizontal sheet would be
# eighty characters per line here, and laying that out by hand is a counting exercise with no
# feedback until it renders wrong. Stacked, each line is one cell wide and a mistake is visible in
# the source.
#
# Digit `d` is the region [0, d/10, 1, 1/10]. There is no text rendering in M1 and there will not be
# until M3's UI system, so a score is drawn as sprites picking cells out of this sheet — which is
# how every game did it before font rasterisers, and which exercises the tilesheet path hard.
#
# The glyphs are 5x7 inside an 8x8 cell, leaving a one-pixel gutter so adjacent digits do not touch.
! . = 00000000   transparent
! # = f2e6c8ff   bone white

# 0
........
..###...
.#...#..
.#..##..
.#.#.#..
.##..#..
.#...#..
..###...

